<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q1.</strong> A module-level <code>tape_lines = []</code> in dashboard.py would appear to "work" briefly, then always show an empty tape. Why?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="Every interaction reruns the whole script — module globals are rebuilt from scratch each time, so the list resets to [] on the very next click.">Each interaction reruns the script, resetting the global to []</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Threading isn't the issue — the script rerun is.">Streamlit runs each widget in its own thread</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Garbage collection is irrelevant; the name is simply re-bound on rerun.">The GC collects lists without references</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="st.code renders whatever it's given; the data vanished before rendering.">st.code can't display lists</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="feedback" hidden></p>
</div>

<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q2.</strong> Why does <code>st.button("↻ Refresh")</code> only fetch the tape once per click instead of on every subsequent rerun?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Buttons carry no debounce — the rerun semantics do the work.">Streamlit debounces buttons for 30 seconds</li>
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="A button returns True only during the single rerun its click caused; the next interaction reruns the script and the button reads False again.">The button returns True only on the click-caused rerun</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="session_state stores the RESULTS, but the fetch gate is the button's return value.">session_state suppresses repeat fetches</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="No cache is involved on this path — and caching a stateful poll would be wrong anyway.">cache_data memoizes the fetch</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="feedback" hidden></p>
</div>

<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q3.</strong> The dashboard deliberately does NOT use ArenaState to read the arena DB. What's the reason?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Speed is fine either way; the issue is what the constructor DOES.">ArenaState is too slow for a dashboard</li>
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="ArenaState's constructor runs guarded ALTER-TABLE migrations — writes. A viewer must never mutate a ledger, so data.py opens its own mode=ro connection that CANNOT write, enforced by SQLite itself (pinned by test).">ArenaState's constructor migrates (writes); the console opens mode=ro instead</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="It imports fine — the choice is about write-safety, not availability.">strategy_arena can't be imported without streamlit</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="compare_strategies IS used — just handed a read-only connection.">compare_strategies requires a raw connection</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="feedback" hidden></p>
</div>

<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q4.</strong> Why do the AppTest console tests auto-skip in the core dev environment?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="They're fast (~2s) — speed isn't the reason.">They're too slow for CI</li>
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="streamlit lives in an OPT-IN extra (`uv sync --extra dashboard`); importorskip makes the suite green without it — which is itself the contract that core installs stay streamlit-free.">streamlit is an opt-in extra; importorskip enforces the streamlit-free core contract</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="AppTest works headlessly — no browser involved.">AppTest needs a real browser</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="They run the real dashboard.py, not a mock.">They only test mocks</li>
